  "about": "Country stamps for the World passport, approved batch by batch on the World Review Country Stamps page (style and plan: ex-pass-country). Each symbol is 14 x 14 rows of 'k' (ink) and '.' (clear).",
  "style": {
    "postmark": "56 x 44 pt: outer rounded rect x 2.5, y 2.5, 51 x 39, radius 5, stroke 2; inner frame x 6, y 6, 44 x 25, radius 3, stroke 0.8; both in the stamp's ink, no fill.",
    "symbol": "14 x 14 pixels centred at x 28, y 18.5, each pixel min(21 / 14, 2.2) = 1.5 pt. About 7 % of ink pixels are left out, chosen by a seeded generator from the country code, so each stamp looks worn in its own way.",
    "name": "Pixel capitals (Pixelify Sans), centred at x 28. One line: baseline 38.6, 5.6 pt (4.6 pt over 10 letters). Two lines: baselines 35.2 and 39.6, 4.4 pt (3.9 pt when a line is over 14 letters). Letter-spacing 0.2.",
    "ink": "One of four inks, #2F6FA3, #B3343A, #2E8B57, #7B4BA8, picked by (first code letter + second code letter) mod 4. Dark mode lightens it 38 % toward white.",
